This falls under the category of account/credential compromise (likely via phishing or weak password hygiene) rather than a direct exploitation of banking infrastructure.

The bank stated the matter was promptly identified and immediate containment measures were implemented, and it maintained that its core banking system remained secure as a forensic probe began. The incident highlights a recurring lesson in cybersecurity: even a single weak link — one employee’s inbox — can expose large volumes of sensitive organizational data, regardless of how secure the core systems are. 

